-- The guarded-chain seed: the two shapes `expandRows` treats ASYMMETRICALLY,
-- and the only fixture that puts either of them under a golden.
--
-- `expandRows`'s own haddock calls that asymmetry "the one thing in this
-- function to test directly", and until this file existed nothing did: every
-- guarded chain in the corpus was a two-arm value-position IF, whose prefix is
-- at most one guard long, so the `j >= 1` half of the prefix loop never ran and
-- `grDisjoint = True` was never taken. Two decisions, one for each half:
--
--   * `loyalty bonus` is a four-arm BRANCH over numeric comparisons. They are
--     not pairwise exclusive by syntax (`guardsDisjoint` is conservative and
--     says so), so arm i materialises the negations of guards 1..i-1 — one for
--     the second arm, TWO for the third, three for the OTHERWISE. Read the
--     golden's `[ … ]` brackets: they are the prefix, and the third arm is
--     where a prefix loop that stopped at j = 0 would show it.
--
--   * `discount rate` is a CONSIDER over a payload-free enum with an OTHERWISE.
--     Distinct constructors against one scrutinee cannot both hold, so
--     `grDisjoint` IS true here and the rows carry NO prefix — but the
--     OTHERWISE still carries the negation of every guard, which is the
--     asymmetry. Its rows lower to `match(V, ctor)`; its OTHERWISE lowers to
--     inequalities against the same constructors, because `RMatch` has no
--     negative form. Note how those print: `\==`, not `=\=`, since `=\=` is
--     ARITHMETIC inequality and raises a type error on an atom in every
--     Prolog-family target (see `L4.Relational.IR`, RCmp).
--
-- The `@ref` and `@nlg` annotations are here because BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R4
-- (workspace anchoring) and R10 (the mandatory `#pred` strings) consume them
-- and nothing else in this corpus carries either, so the two IR fields would go
-- silently empty with every golden still green.
--
-- Each directive below carries its L4-oracle value on the line after it, as a
-- `-- L4 oracle ==>` comment produced by `l4 run tiers.l4` — the differential
-- harness's expectation, kept outside the emitted program per
-- BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R11 and kept in exactly one place per directive.

DECLARE Band IS ONE OF
    bronze
    silver
    gold

DECLARE Member HAS
    band  IS A Band
    years IS A NUMBER

@export
@ref https://example.com/rules/section-3
GIVEN m IS A Member
GIVETH A NUMBER
`discount rate` m MEANS
  CONSIDER m's band
    WHEN gold   THEN 30
    WHEN silver THEN 20
    OTHERWISE        10

@export
GIVEN m IS A Member
GIVETH A NUMBER
`loyalty bonus` m @nlg the loyalty bonus earned by %m%
  MEANS
  BRANCH
    IF m's years AT LEAST 10 THEN 100
    IF m's years AT LEAST 5  THEN 50
    IF m's years AT LEAST 1  THEN 10
    OTHERWISE 0

#EVAL `discount rate` (Member WITH band IS gold, years IS 12)
-- L4 oracle ==> 30

#EVAL `discount rate` (Member WITH band IS bronze, years IS 12)
-- L4 oracle ==> 10

#EVAL `loyalty bonus` (Member WITH band IS silver, years IS 7)
-- L4 oracle ==> 50

#EVAL `loyalty bonus` (Member WITH band IS silver, years IS 0)
-- L4 oracle ==> 0
